response:
Sure!  Loops are used to repeatedly execute a piece of code (like the code inside the loop) until a certain condition is met.  There are three main types of loop:

For loop:

int i = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    doSomething();
}

This loop will execute n times, because the condition "i < n" is true every time it’s true.

While loop:

i = 0;
while (i < n) {
    doSomething();
    i++;
}

This loop will execute until the condition "i < n" is false.

Do loop:

do {
    doSomething();
} while (condition);

This loop is executed once, then the do/while loop continues until the condition is false.

